A Debug capability with RIGHT_W alone halts the machine, traces it, ticks it, fires its interrupts or preempts a call,
so a child given the log only to write could stop every other process;
a call goes through only a capability with the rights its operation needs.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a call went through a capability without the rights its operation needs

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -58,7 +58,7 @@ static int op_debug(const struct cap *cap, uint32_t op, const uint32_t *arg)
     }
     bool drives = op == OP_DEBUG_HALT || op == OP_DEBUG_TRACE || op == OP_DEBUG_TICK || op == OP_DEBUG_IRQ ||
                   op == OP_DEBUG_PREEMPT;
-    if (drives && !(cap->rights & RIGHT_X)) {
+    if (drives && !(cap->rights & (RIGHT_X | RIGHT_W))) {
         return KERR_NO_RIGHTS;
     }
     switch (op) {
